.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt DTFL_COLLECTION_CAPTURE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_collection_capture ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_log_new ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_log_free ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_log_len ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_log_kind ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_log_push_update ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_log_push_progress ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_log_append ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_iter_new ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_iter_free ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_iter_push ,
.Nm dtfl_cdc_iter_next
.Nd capture and replay a differential collection (CDC V2)
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/dd_capture.h
.Ft dtfl_cdc_log *
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_new "const dtfl_type *rec" "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const dtfl_diff *diff"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_free "dtfl_cdc_log *log"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_len "const dtfl_cdc_log *log"
.Ft dtfl_cdc_kind
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_kind "const dtfl_cdc_log *log" "size_t i"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_push_update "dtfl_cdc_log *log" "const void *rec" "size_t reclen" "const uint64_t *time" "const void *diff"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_push_progress "dtfl_cdc_log *log" "const uint64_t *lower" "size_t nlower" "const uint64_t *upper" "size_t nupper" "const uint64_t *count_times" "const size_t *counts" "size_t ncounts"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_append "dtfl_cdc_log *dst" "const dtfl_cdc_log *src" "size_t i"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_capture "dtfl_collection *c" "dtfl_cdc_log *log"
.Ft dtfl_cdc_iter *
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_new "const dtfl_type *rec" "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "const dtfl_diff *diff"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_free "dtfl_cdc_iter *it"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_push "dtfl_cdc_iter *it" "const dtfl_cdc_log *log" "size_t i"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_next "dtfl_cdc_iter *it" "dtfl_cdc_update_fn fn" "void *ctx" "const uint64_t **frontier" "size_t *nfrontier"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions implement the CDC V2 protocol for capturing a differential
collection to a message stream and replaying it, ported from
.Pa differential-dataflow/src/capture.rs .
The protocol records facts about the collection that, once true, stay true:
.Em Updates
messages, each an irrevocable
.Pq data , time , diff
change, and
.Em Progress
messages, each an exact count of distinct updates over a time interval.
Because every message is a monotone statement, a replay reconstructs the
original multiset even when the message stream between capture and replay
duplicates and reorders messages.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_new
creates an empty message log for a collection of records
.Fa rec ,
times of class
.Fa tc
and diffs of class
.Fa diff ,
retaining all three descriptors.
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_free
frees the log and everything in it.
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_len
returns the number of recorded messages, and
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_kind
the kind of message
.Fa i :
.Dv DTFL_CDC_UPDATES
or
.Dv DTFL_CDC_PROGRESS .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_push_update
appends an Updates message holding one
.Pq record , time , diff
triple, and
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_push_progress
appends a Progress message over the interval
.Pq lower , upper
with the given exact per-time counts.
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_append
copies message
.Fa i
of
.Fa src
onto the end of
.Fa dst ,
which is how a captured log is duplicated and reordered before replay.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_capture
is the sink.
It returns a new collection, identical to
.Fa c ,
whose updates and frontier advances are recorded into
.Fa log
as the dataflow runs; attach it to a probe and step the worker to drive the
capture.
The collection
.Fa c
must already be consolidated, since the sink does not consolidate and treats
every record it sees as a true, irrevocable change; pass the output of
.Fn dtfl_collection_consolidate .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_new
creates the replay iterator, the deduplicating and reordering reader of CDC
V2 messages.
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_push
pushes message
.Fa i
of
.Fa log
into the iterator; messages may be pushed in any order and with arbitrary
duplication.
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_next
receives one reconstructed batch: it calls
.Fa fn
once per newly resolved update with its
.Pq record , time , diff ,
sets
.Fa frontier
and
.Fa nfrontier
to the batch's lower bound, and returns
.Dv true ;
it returns
.Dv false
when no new batch is ready.
Call it repeatedly until it returns
.Dv false .
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_free
frees the iterator.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_cdc_log_new ,
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_new
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_capture
return a new handle the caller frees.
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter_next
returns
.Dv true
if it produced a batch,
.Dv false
otherwise.
.Sh NOTES
The data-parallel
.Fn source::build
dataflow of
.Pa capture.rs ,
which reconstructs the stream across workers by running the same dedup and
reorder logic inside four exchange-connected timely operators, is not ported;
.Fn dtfl_cdc_iter
is the single-worker reference it implements and covers the
round-trip-under-duplication-and-reordering guarantee.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_consolidate 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_new 3
.Sh STANDARDS
Ported from
.Lk https://github.com/TimelyDataflow/differential-dataflow differential-dataflow
.Pq differential-dataflow-v0.25.1 , src/capture.rs .
